## 1. Add a play icon in the centre of the black pulse button

**Now:** the home screen's start button is
```html
<button class="pulse" id="startOrb" aria-label="Play"><i></i><b></b></button>
```
- `.pulse i` is the solid black disc (`background:var(--ink)`) that "breathes" (`animation:breathe 1.6s`, scale .86 ↔ 1). On home it also gets a white ring: `#home .pulse i{box-shadow:0 0 0 4px #fff}`.
- `.pulse b` is the expanding halo ring (`animation:halo 1.6s`).
- `.pulse` is `display:grid;place-items:center`, sized `clamp(64px,12vh,96px)` (56px under `max-height:430px`).
- When the selected level is locked, `paintHome()` adds `.locked`: the disc turns grey (`--paper-3`), stops animating, the halo hides, and `::before`/`::after` draw a padlock.

The disc is plain black with nothing on it, so it doesn't read as "play".

**Do:**
- Draw a **white, right-pointing play triangle** centred on the black disc.
  - Add it as a new child element in the markup, e.g. `<button class="pulse" id="startOrb" aria-label="Play"><i></i><b></b><u aria-hidden="true"></u></button>` (any spare inline tag or a `<span class="play-ico">` is fine). **Don't use `::before`/`::after` on `.pulse`** — those pseudo-elements are already taken by the padlock in `.pulse.locked`.
  - Pure CSS, no SVG file, no icon font, no new JS. A CSS triangle is enough, for example: `width:0;height:0;border-style:solid;border-width:<h/2> 0 <h/2> <w>;border-color:transparent transparent transparent #fff`, or a `clip-path:polygon(0 0,100% 50%,0 100%)` box with `background:#fff`. Pick one.
  - **Size:** relative to the button so it scales with the `clamp()` and with the 56px small-height size — roughly 30–34% of the button's width tall, an equilateral-ish triangle. Use `%` / `em` or `calc()` off the button size, not a fixed pixel size.
  - **Optical centre:** a play triangle looks off-centre when its bounding box is centred. Nudge it right by about 6–8% of its own width (e.g. `transform:translateX(8%)` or a small `margin-left`) so it looks centred on the disc.
  - **Layering:** it must sit above the disc (`<i>`) and the halo (`<b>`): `position:relative;z-index:1` (the button is a grid with `place-items:center`, so it centres itself). `pointer-events:none` so clicks still hit the button.
  - **Motion:** the icon should **breathe with the disc** so it never looks detached when the disc shrinks to .86. Easiest: reuse the existing `breathe` keyframes on the icon too (`animation:breathe 1.6s ease-in-out infinite`), keeping the same timing so they stay in phase. If you nudge it with `transform`, don't let the animation's `transform` wipe out the nudge — use `margin-left` for the nudge instead, or a wrapper.
- **Locked state:** when `.pulse.locked`, **hide the play icon** (`display:none`) so only the existing padlock shows. Don't change the padlock.
- **Reduced motion:** add the icon to the existing rule so it stops too: `.pulse i,.pulse b,<icon selector>{animation:none}`. With motion off the disc rests at its unanimated size, so check the icon still looks centred and in proportion.
- **Press feedback:** `.pulse:active{transform:scale(.92)}` scales the whole button, so the icon shrinks with it automatically. Don't add anything for that.
- Keep `aria-label="Play"` on the button. The icon is decorative (`aria-hidden="true"`).
- Don't change the button's size, the disc colour, the white ring, the halo, or `#startLbl` ("play" / "replay · N tries" / "locked") underneath.

